  "review": {
    "note": "Reviewed all direct build, runtime, development and Node declarations and the current upstream release notes/metadata, including candidates outside existing bounds. Hatchling 1.32.4, packaging 26.3, build 1.6.1, mypy 2.4.0, pytest 9.1.1, pytest-xdist 3.8.0, Ruff 0.17.2 and markdownlint-cli2 0.24.0 remain within their declared bounds. The existing rebuild script resolved normally on CPython 3.14.8; both implementation commits passed repository-local Ruff/formatter/strict mypy and Markdown checks with the current tools. All 38 formal-download and CI-bootstrap regression tests passed through the canonical source runner, covering closed Windows download handles, original I/O/cancellation errors, complete dependency-name tokens and bootstrap without importing packaging. Reviewed upstream Python support metadata; pytest-xdist permits Python 3.14 but its classifiers end at 3.13, so metadata acceptance is not upstream execution evidence. Node 24.22.0 meets markdownlint-cli2 0.24.0 requirements. No dependency bounds changed. Native Windows execution is not available on this macOS host; its handle semantics are covered by explicit regressions and retained Windows CI. Formal review and the full candidate gate remain separately required; no publication or deployment is asserted.",
